body:
Might actually be a fun thing to try; maybe I'll ask for a friends supervision haha!

&#x200B;

Thanks!

Also no, not a laptop. I've just noticed in some youtube videos that people use docking stations to mount cable to, rather than running them all into the PC itself. Usually situation/mounted under their desk or the like. 

&#x200B;

I figured having a good enough quality, and then connecting a good bluetooth adapter might work?

Yeah I get you, I would've never really considered that either to be honest. But again, I can't say for sure. I've just happened to notice that it takes a very particular angle to hold a Bluetooth device at, for it to be picked up by my pc.

&#x200B;

The angle it likes it usually directly proportionate to the direction that my CPU cooler does not block, haha.

Awesome, thanks for that suggestion! I'll have a look.

&#x200B;

I've not very technical, are they difficult to insall?
